Model "Coffee Making" {description: "An example of the core and diagram layers."}.

Barista is an environmental physical object.

Brewing is a process {duration_min: 2, duration_expected: 3, duration_max: 5, duration_unit: min}.
Brewing consumes either Ground Coffee or Instant Coffee.
Brewing consumes hot Water.
Brewing yields Coffee.
Brewing requires Coffee Machine.

Coffee is a physical object.

Coffee Beans is a physical object.

Coffee Machine is a physical object.
Coffee Machine is located in Kitchen.

Coffee Making is a process.
Coffee Making zooms into parallel Grinding and Water Heating, and Brewing, in that sequence.

Grinding is a process.
Grinding consumes Coffee Beans.
Grinding yields Ground Coffee.
Barista handles Grinding.

Ground Coffee is a physical object.

Instant Coffee is a physical object.

Kitchen is an environmental physical object.

Water is a physical object.
Water can be cold or hot.
Water is initially cold.
State cold of Water is default.

Water Heating is a process.
Water Heating changes Water from cold to hot.
